# Generated performance baselines. Spec 08.5 wants trustworthy baselines committed, so
# these are ignored by default and a good one is added deliberately with `git add -f`.
# A run can be invalidated by contention, provider rate limits, or a changed dataset,
# and an accidentally committed invalid baseline is worse than none -- it looks
# authoritative. The JSON sidecar feeding the trend section is read from disk, so
# ignoring it costs nothing locally.
docs/perf/*-baseline.md
docs/perf/*-baseline.json

# Local virtualenvs (uv creates .venv; never part of the repo)
.venv/
